@startuml board-rendering
' purpose: StarChessBoard paint contracts — frame,
'   phase ring, fog z-stack, hint/coordinate layers,
'   intent chrome, terrain themes, and glyph states.
' covers: apps/starchess/src/presentation/board/components/StarChessBoard.tsx
' covers: apps/starchess/src/presentation/board/components/StarChessBoard.module.css
' covers: apps/starchess/src/presentation/board/components/LiveStarChessBoard.tsx (veilMoveIds)
' related: _spec/apps/starchess/architecture/reactivity/presentation.md
' related: _spec/apps/starchess/architecture/board-entities.puml
' related: _spec/apps/starchess/architecture/strategy-starchess-board.puml
' related: _spec/apps/starchess/menu-flow.puml
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

title StarChess · Board rendering contracts

component "StarChessBoard.tsx\nsnapshot grid · VisionStrategy pick" as BOARD <<app>>
component "StarChessBoard.module.css\npaint order · overlays · themes" as CSS <<app>>
component "VisionStrategy\nplayer fog | observer dual" as VISION <<app>>
component "fogProjection\ncells · holes · borders" as FOG <<app>>
component "PieceGlyph\nnerd inline | cburnett img" as GLYPH <<app>>

BOARD ARROW_MAIN VISION : strategy pick
BOARD ARROW_MAIN FOG : cells / holes / borders
BOARD ARROW_MAIN GLYPH : unit per square
BOARD ARROW_MAIN CSS : class + data attributes

note as N_FRAME
  Padding plus background builds the frame so
  coordinate labels remain inside the playable
  grid; a box-model border consumed the bottom
  file row. The outer keeps overflow visible
  for the phase outline; the grid clips walk-offs.
end note

note as N_RING
  Phase colors snap instantly while only
  opacity fades, keeping changes on the
  compositor instead of repainting the board
  outline. The ring matches TurnBar chip tones.
end note

note as N_HINT
  Hint arrows ride above the fog veil
  because lesson lines usually address fogged
  squares. Intent chrome, legal rings, and
  destination indicators lift whole squares
  above the veil so guidance remains legible.
end note

note as N_VEIL
  Every enemy mover whose path touches vision
  (fog → sight **and** sight → fog) renders
  beneath the veil, appearing smoothly only
  while crossing lit squares. Their layer forms
  a stacking context that confines animation
  hulls, which would otherwise pierce the veil.
  The veil is **opaque**: a checker ""<pattern>""
  of board tones under 88% fog ink (the same
  colour the old translucent rect composited
  to), so nothing beneath it ever shows through.
  The old ""rgba(…, 0.88)"" rect let 12% of
  anything beneath show, so an enemy sliding
  under the veil ghosted across dark squares.
  Tiles are ""color-mix(fog-ink 88%, board tone)""
  (""--fog-ink: rgb(3,7,10)""); the pattern starts
  on a light corner, true for both viewers
  (a8 and h1 are light).
end note

note as N_UNDERVEIL
  ""LiveStarChessBoard.veilMoveIds"": enemy movers
  whose path crosses the viewer's vision
  (lit ∪ revealed — the veil's own predicate),
  whether they start in fog or in sight. They
  stay in the frame's ""moveCues"" (fog relocation
  + hide squares), but ""CombatOverlayRoot"" drops
  their overlay hull (""hullCues""); the board
  renders them under the opaque veil, shown only
  while on lit squares, out of the fog and into
  it alike. An above-veil hull used to ride over
  the dark: a unit entering the fog stayed
  visible to where it parked.
end note

note as N_COORD
  Rank and file labels live on a board-level
  layer above pieces and fog so theme stacking
  can never bury them. Outlined white lettering
  remains legible across lit and fogged tiles,
  because fog never dims the label plane.
end note

note as N_GATE
  Concealed enemy units never leak through
  intent rings, canister badges, or aura marks;
  those marks paint while the unit stays hidden.
  Mines appear only on lit squares, and burning
  damage cues obey the same visibility gate.
end note

note as N_GRASS
  Wildgrass dark tiles overflow onto stone
  paths, so color lives on a ragged overlay
  beneath the pieces. Seven staggered rotations
  keep texture varied without disturbing
  interaction overlays.
end note

note as N_CSS
  Board chrome selects structural square
  attributes, never test identifiers, so test
  hooks stay out of stylesheets. Density travels
  through compact and class properties into
  each heads-up display module.
end note

N_FRAME .. CSS
N_RING .. CSS
N_HINT .. CSS
N_VEIL .. BOARD
N_UNDERVEIL .. BOARD
N_COORD .. CSS
N_GATE .. BOARD
N_GRASS .. CSS
N_CSS .. CSS

@enduml
